  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>morse.prosigns</keyword>
  <short_description>The common Morse procedural signals.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>morse.prosigns()</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>p = morse.prosigns()</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input />
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>p</param_name>
      <param_description>an N-by-3 cell array: the prosign name, its bracketed text form and its dot/dash code.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>Prosigns are procedural signals sent as several letters run together, with no gap between them. In text they are written between angle brackets, and <b>morse.encode</b> turns a bracketed group into the run-together code: morse.encode('&lt;AR&gt;') is '.-.-.'. Called with no output, morse.prosigns prints the common ones (AR, AS, BT, CT, KN, SK, SN, SOS).</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography />
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data><![CDATA[morse.prosigns()
morse.encode('R RN <AR>')]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
